'''Mark Samuel Cooper'''  (born February 14, 1960) is an American former professional [[American football|football]] player who was a [[Guard (American football)|guard]] in the [[National Football League]] (NFL) for the [[Denver Broncos]] and the [[Tampa Bay Buccaneers]]. He [[Starting lineup|started]] for the Broncos in [[Super Bowl XXI]]. Cooper played [[college football]] for the [[Miami Hurricanes football|Miami Hurricanes]], where he was a Second-team All-South Independent ([[1982 All-South Independent football team|1982]])
